== evidence 1: capacity model in the design review (2026-05-11)
CPU per request (profiled at low load): 4.0 ms; worker threads: 4
capacity = 4 / 4.0 ms = 1000 req/s; target load 400 req/s -> utilisation 40 %
conclusion in the review: "plenty of headroom; no queueing expected"

== evidence 2: load test, 120 s per row, open-loop Poisson arrivals, gateway timing
 req/s   p50 ms   p99 ms    max ms    CPU % | thread states of the 4 workers (% of time)
                                            |  running  blocked (mutex)   idle
   100     3.19    18.80      38.0      10% |      10%               1%    89%
   200     3.98    21.72      42.8      20% |      20%               6%    75%
   300     5.32    28.59      55.6      30% |      30%              14%    56%
   400     8.70    46.91      84.6      39% |      39%              28%    33%
   450    15.53    94.43     128.2      45% |      45%              38%    18%
   480    34.29   297.56     344.9      48% |      48%              44%     8%

("CPU %" is the share of the 4 workers' time spent running code;
 "blocked (mutex)" is time a worker held a request but waited for a lock.)
